ny claim that turns on WHEN or by WHOM something was said, or whether it is still the current framing. Witness-depth sections below already carry full provenance.\n\nThis entry is BOUNDED — the whole graph is deliberately not inlined. Every node is reachable within a bounded number of expands: before concluding the perspective is silent on your subject, check the map and coverage, then expand the door whose axis would hold it (^Thematic for topics and areas, ^People for anyone, ^Documents for a call or memory, ^Unplaced for loose positions). Absence becomes signal only after the relevant door shows nothing.\n\n# The map — this graph's richest ground (top fidelity band)\n\n\n# Coverage — narrated, from four directions\n\n\n# Doors — pick an axis\n\n[ ^Thematic — every area (0) by name ] [ ^People 2 ] [ ^Dimensions — 0 axes ] [ ^Documents 1 ] [ ^Unplaced 0 ]\nEach door expands to a complete axis: aswritten_expand(iris=[\"Thematic\"]) — same coords as this perspective. Nothing in the graph is outside every door.\n\n# Focus: Second version — reviewer note by Xena ExpertGH, a revision/overwrite of a prior first version (witness depth — per-call section)\n\n### Actor_XenaExpertgh — Xena ExpertGH\ntype: Actor\nwitnessed: 20260926\nXena ExpertGH\n\n### Sample_20260926_1_E2EOverwrite1790417168938_hee49df94289f\ntype: Sample\nwitnessed: 20260926\nFirst version\n\n### ns__Decision_DiagnosticFirst\ntype: ns__Decision\nXena: 'Every engagement starts with a diagnostic phase. Never propose solutions before understanding the system.' Two weeks, $5K, 8+ stakeholder interviews.\nDiagnostic First Methodology\nunder: ns__Strategy\n\n### ns__Actor_XenaGithubber\ntype: ns__Actor\nIndependent consultant specializing in knowledge mapping and organizational diagnostics.\nXena Githubber\n\n\n### Sample_20260926_1_E2EOverwrite1790417168938_hee49df94289f\ntype: Sample\nwitnessed: 20260926\nFirst version\n\nchildren (witness depth):\n\n### Expr_20260926_1_E2EOverwrite1790417168938_hee49df94289f